                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "LeoWu-wiwynn",
                        "email": "leo.wu.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "LeoWu-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi, @patrick@stwcx.xyz @amithash@meta.com\n\nSince this patch is currently blocked waiting for the dependency in [phosphor-dbus-interfaces (#77319)](https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/77319) to merge, the current CI build failure is expected.\n\nHowever, I'd like to request an early conceptual review on the core logic before the dependency gets in. Specifically, I'm looking for feedback on:\n\n1. Is this the appropriate file/layer to intercept the NIC inventory events? \n2. Does the logic for detecting and handling NIC plug-in/plug-out correctly align with expectations?\n\nAny early advice or suggestions on the approach would be greatly appreciated. Thanks!"
                }
            ],
